title: "Structure Beyond Length: What Human Raters, LLM Judges and Reward Models Reward in Model Answers"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "working draft"
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com/structure_beyond_length.html
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/structure-beyond-length
keywords: [llm evaluation, reward models, llm-as-judge, human preference, style bias, chatbot arena]
abstract: >
  Four public preference corpora read with one fixed structural instrument (Linguistic Kernel v19),
  comparing the two answers to the same prompt. Human raters reward a structure direction beyond length
  until both answers already carry the 2024 style; an LLM judge and three open reward models used in
  training keep rewarding it, also beyond Arena's own style-control features. Pre-registered, with all
  derived data and scripts.
